From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5018: ack SMP2P restarts of the WCSS

Without qcom,smp2p-feature-ssr-ack the Q6 starts once per boot. Any
later start - after a firmware crash, or after the ath11k driver was
unbound and bound again - ends in

  qcom-wcss-secure-pil cd00000.remoteproc: start timed out
  remoteproc remoteproc0: can't start rproc q6wcss: -110

The Q6 does come up: the smp2p interrupt fires during the attempt, but
"ready" never follows, because the firmware waits for the host to
acknowledge the restart. The vendor device tree for the IPQ5018 has the
property, as the IPQ6018 has here since "soc: qcom: fix smp2p ack on
ipq6018", which describes the same failure.

On an Archer AX55 v1 with it the Q6 is up again 0.1 s after an unbind
and bind, and 0.2 s after a firmware crash.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
@@ -1217,6 +1217,7 @@
 
 		wcss_smp2p_out: master-kernel {
 			qcom,entry-name = "master-kernel";
+			qcom,smp2p-feature-ssr-ack;
 			#qcom,smem-state-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
